@param threadId: String
@param summoning: Boolean = true
@if(summoning)
    <%-- "Summoning the room…": the create-time room summon is still routing on a worker (the dispatcher's
         "who replies" LLM call). Self-polls GET /threads/{id}/room every second; that endpoint answers with
         whatever the room has produced — drafts still in flight, replies that already settled, or both —
         retargeting the whole reply list so the server render replaces it wholesale. Until then it
         re-emits this poller (replacing only itself, so a note posted mid-wait survives), and emits
         nothing once a summon ends having produced nothing at all, so htmx stops.
         data-empty-state mirrors the static "waiting" state's hook. --%>
    <div data-empty-state="summoning"
         hx-get="/threads/${threadId}/room"
         hx-trigger="every 1s"
         hx-swap="outerHTML">Summoning the room…</div>
@endif
